<title>USA: TVA cuts output at Sequoyah 2 Tenn. nuclear unit.</title>
<headline>TVA cuts output at Sequoyah 2 Tenn. nuclear unit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>TVA Nuclear's 1,148 megawatt (MW) Sequoyah 2 nuclear unit was taken off line for repairs, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Monday in its plant status report.</p>
<p>The unit, in Soddy-Daisy, Tenn., was operating at 20 percent of capacity while operators made repairs in the main transformer.</p>
<p>No further details were available as to when the unit would resume full power.</p>
<p>The adjacent unit 1, also rated at 1,148 MW, continued to run at full power.</p>
<p>((--H McCulloch, New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
